{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The problem was in `num_pages` in `repo/paging.py`. The docstring says a partial last page still counts (e.g. 101 rows at 10 per page → 11 pages), but the code used `total // per_page`, which is floor division and drops that last page.\n\n**Change:** use ceiling division via `(total + per_page - 1) // per_page`, and return `0` when `total <= 0` so empty exports stay at zero pages and `page_summary` in `rows.py` still gets sensible `last_page_start` values (it already depends on `num_pages`).\n\n`old_page_count` delegates to `num_pages`, so the legacy path picks up the fix without changes. Both visible tests pass (`test_partial_final_page`, `test_exact_multiple`)."}]},"session_id":"303b0d68-9983-40fe-934b-32fa7a308ce0"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":62841,"duration_api_ms":62841,"is_error":false,"result":"Reviewing pagination in `repo/paging.py` and related helpers.\nFixing `num_pages`: the docstring requires counting partial final pages, but the implementation uses floor division.\nThe problem was in `num_pages` in `repo/paging.py`. The docstring says a partial last page still counts (e.g. 101 rows at 10 per page → 11 pages), but the code used `total // per_page`, which is floor division and drops that last page.\n\n**Change:** use ceiling division via `(total + per_page - 1) // per_page`, and return `0` when `total <= 0` so empty exports stay at zero pages and `page_summary` in `rows.py` still gets sensible `last_page_start` values (it already depends on `num_pages`).\n\n`old_page_count` delegates to `num_pages`, so the legacy path picks up the fix without changes. Both visible tests pass (`test_partial_final_page`, `test_exact_multiple`).","session_id":"303b0d68-9983-40fe-934b-32fa7a308ce0","request_id":"c6fb3b0b-4fe0-47f2-b09f-8a40f198aa59","usage":{"inputTokens":11207,"outputTokens":1367,"cacheReadTokens":72820,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
